Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:58:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?HTDESIGNER-55:=20label=20Alignment;=20=E6=94=B9?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E5=9B=9E=20DFM=20gives=20an=20AutoSize=3DFalse=20label=20the?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20.dfm's=20own=20size=20(0.55.0)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A porting gap the page generator leaves: it ignores a label's AutoSize =
False and its Alignment. Setup.Contact's labDelayStatus is 273 x 25 and
centred in BCB6, but drawn width:auto and left-aligned on the page, so its
text sits somewhere else than on the machine's old screen.
- properties panel: Alignment for labels (taLeftJustify / taCenter /
  taRightJustify = text-align; left = no declaration), compared with the
  DFM (a TLabel's default is taLeftJustify)
- AutoSize = False from the DFM (the list's reset, 改回 DFM, the panel's ↺)
  now writes the .dfm's own width / height -- not the size the text makes
  now -- so one reset makes the label match; the list notes that size
- lib: dfmEditValues.alignment, the AutoSize row's reset carries size,
  resetItemsOf passes it on; the host passes it to the probe

Tests: lib (the default; a centred AutoSize=False label drawn auto -> both
rows, the reset with 273 x 25), probe (Alignment -> text-align:center and
the look says taCenter; AutoSize off with a size -> exactly that size), real
VS Code (Setup.Contact labDelayStatus: 改回 DFM -> 273 x 25 centred in the
source in one step, ONE undo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
